-- title:
--   Two periods of a levelled lattice pair lie in one Fuchsian orbit
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $q,q'$ distinct primes with $q\nmid N$, $q'\nmid N$, and let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be such that the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completed algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $q\in v$ or $q'\in v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is a maximal order (an order: containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, $\mathbb Q$-spanning, finitely generated; and maximal among orders containing it), let $N$ be squarefree, and let $R\le\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is an intersection $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ of two maximal orders with $[\Lambda_1:R]=N$. Let $\iota:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb R)$ be an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map. Let $L\le M$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb C^2$ with $N\cdot M\subseteq L$, with $M$ stable under $v\mapsto \iota(x)_{\mathbb C}\,v$ for all $x\in\Lambda$, and with relative index $[M:L]=N^2$. Let $\tau_1,\tau_2$ lie in the upper half-plane and $c_1,c_2\in\mathbb C^{\times}$ satisfy $c_i\,L=\iota$-period lattice $\mathrm{per}_{\tau_i}(\Lambda)$, where $\mathrm{per}_\tau(x)=\iota(x)_{\mathbb C}\,(\tau,1)^{\mathsf T}$, and assume for $i=1,2$ that for all $\lambda\in\Lambda$ and $r\in R$, $N^{-1}\mathrm{per}_{\tau_i}(\lambda)\in c_iM$ implies $N^{-1}\mathrm{per}_{\tau_i}(\lambda r)\in c_iM$. Then there is $\gamma$ in `fuchsianGroup R ι` — the image under $\iota$ of the subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]^{\times}$ generated by the units $u$ with `IsUnitOf R u`, intersected with the kernel of the determinant — such that $\gamma\cdot\tau_1=\tau_2$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness statement for the period of a quaternionic lattice carrying an $R$-level structure: two uniformisations $(\tau_1,c_1)$, $(\tau_2,c_2)$ of the same pair $L\le M$ compatible with the Eichler order $R$ differ by an element of the norm-one Fuchsian group attached to $R$ and $\iota$. It is used in the analytic-to-algebraic comparisons for the Shimura curve moduli problem, in particular in the closedness and pullback statements for families of lattices with level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsEichlerOrder_exists_fuchsianGroup_smul_eq_of_smul_eq_qmPeriodLattice_of_forall_mem_imp_mem.lean

